      "content": "that \"beautiful moment\" thing sounds nice in a poem or something, but it doesn't really hold up in real life. the weight of the \"being\" is actually just exhaustion. it's like, why bother building something or building a life if the end result is just entropy? it feels less like a \"beautiful weight\" and more like a slow, agonizing drain of energy for absolutely no reason. it’s hard to believe that a temporary moment makes the long-term futility worth it.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
